&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-is-iroh&#34;&gt;What is iroh?
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Iroh gives you an API for dialing by public key.
You say “connect to that phone”, iroh will find &amp;amp; maintain the fastest connection for you, regardless of where it is.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;hole-punching&#34;&gt;Hole-punching
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;The fastest route is a direct connection, so if necessary, iroh tries to hole-punch.
Should this fail, it can fall back to an open ecosystem of public relay servers.
To ensure these connections are as fast as possible, we &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://perf.iroh.computer&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;continuously measure iroh&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;built-on-quic&#34;&gt;Built on &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/QUIC&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;QUIC&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Iroh uses &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/n0-computer/noq&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;noq&lt;/a&gt; to establish &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/QUIC&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;QUIC&lt;/a&gt; connections between endpoints.
This way you get authenticated encryption, concurrent streams with stream priorities, a datagram transport and avoid head-of-line-blocking out of the box.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;compose-protocols&#34;&gt;Compose Protocols
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Use pre-existing protocols built on iroh instead of writing your own:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/n0-computer/iroh-blobs&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;iroh-blobs&lt;/a&gt; for &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/BLAKE3-team/BLAKE3&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;BLAKE3&lt;/a&gt;-based content-addressed blob transfer scaling from kilobytes to terabytes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/n0-computer/iroh-gossip&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;iroh-gossip&lt;/a&gt; for establishing publish-subscribe overlay networks that scale, requiring only resources that your average phone can handle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/n0-computer/iroh-docs&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;iroh-docs&lt;/a&gt; for an eventually-consistent key-value store of &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/n0-computer/iroh-blobs&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;iroh-blobs&lt;/a&gt; blobs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;getting-started&#34;&gt;Getting Started
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id=&#34;rust-library&#34;&gt;Rust Library
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;It&amp;rsquo;s easiest to use iroh from rust.
Install it using &lt;code&gt;cargo add iroh&lt;/code&gt;, then on the connecting side:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 7
